# Personal GitHub identity (required)

This repository is personal. Every commit, push, fetch, and `gh` command uses **jorsisu** only. Never skip this for convenience, and never fall back to the active or work account.

- GitHub user: `jorsisu`
- Commit name: `Jorge Galarza`
- Commit email: `jgalarzah@gmail.com`
- Remote: `https://github.com/jorsisu/jor-stack.git`

Do not use `Jorge-Galarza_vail`, `jorgegalarzaverndale`, `Jorge.Galarza+vail@vailresorts.com`, or any other work identity.

Before every commit, `git config --local user.email` must be `jgalarzah@gmail.com` and `user.name` must be `Jorge Galarza`. If either local value is missing or wrong, restore only this repo (never `--global`):

```bash
git config --local user.name "Jorge Galarza"
git config --local user.email "jgalarzah@gmail.com"
```

Stop and do not commit if the author would be anyone else.

Before every `git push`, `git pull`, `git fetch`, or `gh` command:

- Do not run `gh auth switch`.
- Do not change `~/.gitconfig` or the active `gh` account.
- Leave the local GitHub credential helper pinned to `jorsisu`. If it is missing, restore it:

```bash
git config --local credential.https://github.com.username jorsisu
git config --local --replace-all credential.https://github.com.helper ""
git config --local --add credential.https://github.com.helper '!f() { echo "username=jorsisu"; echo "password=$(gh auth token --hostname github.com --user jorsisu)"; }; f'
```

- Run `gh` with the personal token and do not print that token:

```bash
GH_TOKEN="$(gh auth token --hostname github.com --user jorsisu)" gh ...
```

If the token command fails, stop and ask the user to run `gh auth login -h github.com` for `jorsisu`. Do not use another logged-in account.
